group render
note The io-fonts crate: the monospaced font families installed on this machine, for the settings box's font list. Fonts::scan walks the system and user font folders of macOS, Linux and Windows (folders that do not exist are skipped, six levels deep at most) and reads only the table directory, the name table and two small headers of each .ttf, .otf, .ttc or .otc file, never a whole file, so a scan of a few hundred files takes a fraction of a second; the GUI still runs it on a background thread the first time the box opens. A face counts as monospaced when its post table says fixed pitch or its OS/2 panose says monospaced Latin text; families whose names start with a dot (macOS system faces) are left out. Each family keeps its regular face when it has one. read hands the renderer the whole file and the face index.

